   "Sridhar Kora succeeded the longstanding hostel office in-charge, Sri B. Lakshmi Narayana. Having previously worked at institutions such as ICFAI Business School and BITS Pilani Hyderabad (for 8 months) as a hostel in-charge, he holds a diploma in mechanical engineering and an MBA. Upon joining in 2018, he underwent a 10-day orientation program. [One sentence removed by the team for privacy.] Drawing from his mechanical engineering background, he has actively spearheaded technical and operational innovations across the palash hostel.",
   "Earlier, when the institute catered to only a few hundred students, solar water heaters alone met the campus hot water demand. As student strength grew, however, this capacity proved insufficient. Electric geysers were deployed for a period, but their inconvenient heating time caused bottlenecks during the morning rush. Consequently, the team explored alternatives, visiting BITS Pilani Hyderabad to examine innovative heat pump systems, which were subsequently installed on campus and permanently resolved the issue.",
   "LAN connectivity was also expanded across the campus as bandwidth and access requirements grew. Older furniture, such as S-type wire-mesh chairs, was replaced with ergonomic cushioned seating. Recently, the D-block washrooms were completely renovated ahead of the UG2k25 batch. Room occupancy has transitioned over time from single occupancy to double sharing, and now to triple sharing, which frequently leads to day-to-day roommate friction. During vacation periods, visiting project interns are accommodated in six-sharing rooms equipped with bunk beds - a rather intensive setup.",
   "During the COVID-19 pandemic, both classes and examinations transitioned to the CodeTantra platform, making IIITH the first institution in Hyderabad to shift entirely to an online operational mode."
